    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f2068935-7e26-51c9-822c-fbfed7d4ffb0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $3\\text{rd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $3\\text{rd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows of $A$ are $-4,$ $6,$ and $6$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-4+6+6=8.$",
